  "question": {
    "text": "A large flat metal surface has a uniform charge density <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> . An electron of mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> and charge <math><mi>ρ</mi></math> leaves the surface at the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> with speed&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>u</mi></math> and returns to it at point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>. Disregarding gravity the maximum value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AB</mi></math> is<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/WhatsApp_Image_2020-08-24_at_1.59.06_PM.jpeg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 139px;\" />",
    "image": null
